## Optimisations vs. one-shot prompts

- **DeepSeek for copy.** Long-form prose at ~10x lower cost than Sonnet. Quality is fine for one-page sites.
- **gpt-image-1 for hero.** Renders text well, follows brief reliably.
- **Direct deploy via Wrangler.** Cloudflare Pages via Wrangler API — faster and more reliable than wrangler CLI in CI.
- **Schema generated programmatically.** Not via LLM. Deterministic, valid, faster.
- **Job-spec orchestrator.** One JSON file per build, append-only log. Reproducible, debuggable.

## Architectural considerations

- **EMD without quality is junk.** Without good copy, schema, internal links, an EMD ranks for nothing. Don't think of this as "deploy the domain" — think of it as "minimum viable money page."
- **Watch for AI-content detection.** Search engines are increasingly down-ranking obviously AI-generated content. Your prompt + your post-processing matter.
- **Schema markup is high-leverage.** A correct LocalBusiness, Product, or Article schema gets you rich results. Worth building in.
- **Don't deploy junk to a fresh domain.** First impressions matter — Google indexes the first version, and that becomes the baseline trust signal.
- **Hero images cost.** Each gpt-image-1 generation has a per-image cost ([see OpenAI pricing](https://openai.com/api/pricing)). At scale this adds up — cache aggressively, reuse where avatar is similar.

## What this skill does NOT include

- Pre-built page templates (you provide).
- Niche-specific copy strategies (you provide).
- Domain purchasing — that's `domain-finder-agent` or manual.
- Anything that violates a search engine's webmaster guidelines (cloaking, sneaky redirects, link-scheme manipulation).
- Token handling guidance — store all CDN/registrar/API keys in environment variables or a secrets manager; use least-privilege scopes; never log them.

